AndroidManifest.xml edits (insert these lines into android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml)

1) Add the following permission lines as direct children of the <manifest> element (near the top):

    <!-- Location permissions -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" />
    <!-- For background location on Android 10+ -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION" />

2) Update the <application> tag to include foreground service type if you plan to use a foreground service for continuous tracking:

    <application
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:foregroundServiceType="location">

Replace existing <application ...> start tag with the one above (preserve other attributes). Remove the added attribute if you don't use foreground services.

Notes:
- These edits assume you generated the Android folder via `flutter create .`.
- After applying, rebuild the app and test on device to confirm runtime permission requests behave correctly.
